# R5 acceptance transcript: canonical Merkle decomposition.
#
# R4 |- R5. Large objects gain a canonical decomposition.
#
# A large map gains a second, equally canonical spelling: a tree of chunks
# whose boundaries are a pure function of the extensional entry set -- a key
# closes its chunk exactly when its own artifact digest says so. The same
# entries decompose identically whatever order they arrived in; an edit
# re-hashes the chunks on one path and shares every other subtree; and the
# root is named by naming its children, not by re-encoding the map.

